{%- comment -%}
  App Embed — "Images per language": swaps a product's images for the
  replacement the merchant set for the visitor's language (and market) in the
  app. Shopify cannot store a product image per language, so this is the one
  place the swap can happen; og:image and the JSON-LD image list do the same
  server-side through snippets/cp-localized-image.liquid.

  Data: `custom.localized_media` (json) — see the snippet's header for the
  shape. The app validates `o` and `u` before it writes them, but anything
  with metafield access (another app, an import, the admin's metafield
  editor) can write this value too, so the <style> never trusts it: an `o`
  carrying a quote, an angle bracket or a backslash is skipped there (it could
  otherwise close the selector or the <style> element). The JSON island goes
  through `json`, which escapes it.

  Videos (PLAN_LOCALIZED_IMAGES §7) ride the same island: the asset swaps a
  `<video>`'s sources and an `<iframe>`'s embed address. Only their POSTER is
  hidden pre-paint (`p`, when the replacement has a poster of its own) — a
  player is not painted before playback anyway. An entry with nothing to hide
  still loads the asset, which is why the island is printed whenever the
  visitor's language (and market) has an entry at all.

  Pre-paint: the <style> hides every <img> showing an original that has a
  replacement here, BEFORE the page paints, so the visitor never sees the
  original flash and swap. assets/localized-media.js rewrites the URLs and
  marks each image, which shows it again. The inline timer is the fail-safe:
  if the script never runs, nothing stays hidden for longer than 3 seconds.

  Liquid budget: this block and the snippet are all the Liquid the feature
  owns; every decision that can be made in the browser is made in the asset.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lm = product.metafields.custom.localized_media.value
  assign loc = request.locale.iso_code | downcase
  assign mk = localization.market.id | append: ''
  assign sel = ''
  assign has = false
  for e in lm.e
    if e.l == loc
      if e.k == blank or e.k == mk
        assign has = true
        assign f = e.o
        if e.x != blank
          assign f = ''
          if e.u != blank
            assign f = e.p
          endif
        endif
        if f != blank
        unless f contains '"' or f contains '<' or f contains '>' or f contains '\'
        assign sel = sel | append: ',img[src*="/' | append: f | append: '"]:not([data-cp-lm]),img[srcset*="/' | append: f | append: '"]:not([data-cp-lm])'
        endunless
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if has -%}
{%- if sel != '' -%}
<style id="cp-lm-prehide">{{ sel | remove_first: ',' }}{visibility:hidden}</style>
<script>setTimeout(function(){var s=document.getElementById('cp-lm-prehide');s&&s.remove()},3000)</script>
{%- endif -%}
<script type="application/json" id="cp-lm-data">{"l":{{ loc | json }},"k":{{ mk | json }},"e":{{ lm.e | json }}}</script>
<script src="{{ 'localized-media.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Media per language",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows the product images and videos you replaced per language or market in the app."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
